fix(driver-app): unblock UI when Google Fonts (Cairo) is slow/blocked

User report: "delivery app isn't working — welcome screen never loads
(blank/red error) AND login/OTP doesn't work".

Root cause: driver-app/_layout.tsx gates the entire UI on `useFonts({Cairo_*})`
from @expo-google-fonts/cairo. In the proxied iframe environment Cairo can't be
fetched from Google Fonts; fontfaceobserver eventually rejects with a
"12000ms timeout exceeded" unhandled rejection (visible in browser console
logs) and `fontsLoaded` never flips true, so the layout returns the blank red
View forever. That blocks welcome, which blocks login, OTP, register —
matching both symptoms exactly.

Fix:
- driver-app/app/_layout.tsx: also unblock when `useFonts` returns an error,
  AND add a 2-second fallback timer that flips an `fontsTimeout` flag so the
  app renders with the system font even if useFonts hangs. Now the gate is
  `fontsLoaded || fontsError || fontsTimeout` instead of only `fontsLoaded`.
  (User-app already had equivalent handling.)

Verification: ran an end-to-end test against /driver/ — welcome renders,
"J'ai déjà un compte" → login → POST /admin-api/otp/send 200 → OTP screen →
verify with fake code returns the expected 400 with the correct error UI →
"Commencer" → register screen renders.
